WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.950
Gauntlet tests, attacks and guards your AI agents. Here is every feature.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.617
Simulated customers, with personas and goals, talk to your agent.

3
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:19.583
The report shows the pass rate, and the failing conversation.

4
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:23.850
Every verdict cites the exact event as evidence.

5
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.850
Each role has its own model.

6
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:33.350
Compare against a baseline: flips show what got better or worse.

7
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:41.717
Reliability shows how often it passes every time. Failures cluster.

8
00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:46.217
Replay a failing episode against a new version.

9
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:53.617
The migration report compares versions.

10
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:57.117
Reviewers label episodes blind.

11
00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:03.283
Labels calibrate rubrics. Until then, a rubric cannot gate a release.

12
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:06.250
A campaign attacks the agent.

13
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:12.017
It found a critical hole, with evidence and SARIF export.

14
00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:16.283
Posture shows what was tested.

15
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:22.083
Scan MCP servers and lint agent code, right in the terminal.

16
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.717
A suggested rule, tested offline.

17
00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:31.017
Enforce it, then verify the attacks now fail.

18
00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:36.283
The gateway logs decisions. Risky calls wait for approval.

19
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:40.650
Pinning catches an MCP rug pull instantly.

20
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.017
In CI, the gate fails the build.

21
00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:49.917
Results land as a pull request comment, plus a badge.

22
00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:55.883
Ingest production traces. Personal data is redacted on arrival.

23
00:01:55.933 --> 00:02:00.950
Failure mining drafts new scenarios from real failures.

24
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.717
Packs: enterprise access probes, banking, tau-bench and AgentDojo importers.

25
00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:12.083
SLOs, schedules, alerts, and change impact.

26
00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:17.183
Readiness gives a go or no-go, with a signed evidence pack.

27
00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:24.150
Claude Code drives Gauntlet over MCP: list agents, start a small, capped run.

28
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.517
It polls until the run finishes.

29
00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:34.517
Then it summarises the results, and the cost.

30
00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:40.850
The public arena: attack a hardened agent.

31
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:45.517
Benchmarks publish our own numbers, good or bad.
